1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:03,396
Yuck!

2
00:00:03,446 --> 00:00:05,744
This drop of seawater is salty,

3
00:00:05,794 --> 00:00:07,788
while river water is fresh.

4
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:09,731
But why is the sea salty?

5
00:00:10,555 --> 00:00:11,945
Noah tastes the stream…

6
00:00:11,995 --> 00:00:12,883
it isn't salty!

7
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:13,384
And yet,

8
00:00:13,434 --> 00:00:16,688
every stream and river flows all the way to the sea.

9
00:00:17,472 --> 00:00:18,986
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:21,515 --> 00:00:22,051
Mini mode!

11
00:00:22,101 --> 00:00:23,868
Rain is just a tiny bit acidic.

12
00:00:23,918 --> 00:00:28,557
So, flowing over rocks, it wears them down and carries away tiny grains of salt,

13
00:00:28,607 --> 00:00:30,366
too few to taste in the river!

14
00:00:31,185 --> 00:00:33,159
But day after day, for millions of years,

15
00:00:33,209 --> 00:00:34,887
rivers bring their salt to the sea.

16
00:00:34,937 --> 00:00:37,355
Then the water goes back up into the sky as vapor,

17
00:00:37,405 --> 00:00:38,194
without the salt…

18
00:00:38,244 --> 00:00:39,479
which stays and piles up.

19
00:00:40,284 --> 00:00:41,872
And at the bottom of the sea,

20
00:00:41,922 --> 00:00:45,148
water heated by volcanoes comes back out full of minerals…

21
00:00:45,198 --> 00:00:45,713
more salt!

22
00:00:45,763 --> 00:00:46,673
So a glass of sea

23
00:00:46,723 --> 00:00:48,587
water holds almost two spoonfuls.

24
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:51,034
Two spoonfuls of salt in a glass:

25
00:00:51,084 --> 00:00:52,504
that's the taste of the sea.

26
00:00:52,554 --> 00:00:54,867
And since the water always leaves without it,

27
00:00:54,917 --> 00:00:56,177
the sea will stay salty.

28
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,840
And that's why the sea is salty.

29
00:01:00,505 --> 00:01:03,467
Rain wears down rocks, rivers carry the salt to the sea,

30
00:01:03,517 --> 00:01:05,239
and the water leaves without it.

31
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:09,515
With an adult: put very salty water in a plate,

32
00:01:09,565 --> 00:01:10,235
in the sun.

33
00:01:10,285 --> 00:01:11,739
When the water is gone…

34
00:01:11,789 --> 00:01:13,358
the salt is still there!

35
00:01:14,141 --> 00:01:16,195
And why does the sea rise and fall?

36
00:01:16,245 --> 00:01:17,447
The answer tomorrow.
